From d5da4177f4aec1dd14d5342f802ed82420c6840f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael <michael@lingxia.app>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:01:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(tree): keep no layout from a sizing pass

Flexbox baseline alignment lays out a row's children with `RunMode::PerformLayout` even when
the row itself is only being sized (`RunMode::ComputeSize` for the cross axis or both axes,
as when a column measures a row's height at a min- or max-content width). Those layouts were
stored, as was each child's final-layout cache entry. On a later layout the row's own
final-layout cache hit skipped its subtree, so rounding published the sizing pass's geometry:
a text laid out at max-content on one line inside a narrower cell, or a zero-basis cell at
its min-content width.

`TaffyView` now counts the `ComputeSize` calls enclosing the current one, and inside them
stores no unrounded layout and no final-layout cache entry. Nothing reads stored layouts while
computing, so sizing results are unchanged.
